1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,900
[Shortwave static & carrier acquisition]

2
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:04,250
This is GOR-9. This is GOR-9.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,200
[Harmonic crystal signal-lock chime]

4
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:14,170
Galactic Outpost Radio, broadcasting from the High Basalt Shelf Tower
on Asteroid 3-5-1, 42,100 AU out in Oort Cloud Sector 9.

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:20,520
Fourteen-two-eighty-five kilohertz upper sideband.
Zero-four-hundred Galactic Coordinated.

6
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:29,448
On the Van Allen VA-4 Propagation and Power Console—
brought to you by Van Allen and Sons Switchgear of Ceres Foundry Seven:

7
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:36,587
Comet K-Four's ion tail is sweeping azimuth two-twelve,
opening a clean 24 MHz skip corridor into the Jovian moons.

8
00:00:36,627 --> 00:00:41,491
Closer to home, a 60 kV triboelectric dust squall
has engulfed Relay KZ9-Omega—

9
00:00:41,531 --> 00:00:48,257
raising our lower usable frequency by 4 MHz and arcing
across the number-four Belt-Master marzelvane bushing.

10
00:00:48,297 --> 00:00:50,430
Expect SINPO two-three-two-two-two.

11
00:00:51,850 --> 00:01:01,016
On the Dilithium Bus: Grade-B Dilithium pellets rose four percent
on the Ceres Exchange following a dragline cable slowdown at Silicate Quarry 44-K.

12
00:01:01,056 --> 00:01:09,725
With our Van Allen Ring-Bake corona de-icer pulling an extra 4.5 kilowatts,
we are stepping Reactor Two down to 12 kilowatts after midnight—

13
00:01:09,765 --> 00:01:14,204
Dormitory Wing B should plug in their Van Allen Cryo-Toast foot-warmers.

14
00:01:14,244 --> 00:01:25,090
Meanwhile, our monthly pellet and vacuum-tube tender remains impounded at Quarantine Buoy Twelve
after customs misfiled replacement oscillator tubes as fermented brine tubers.

15
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:31,197
Turning to the Hauser Dynamics Mark-Four Receiver and Galaxy Atlas:

16
00:01:31,237 --> 00:01:38,540
Preset Two—Titan-Minor, 3,890 kilohertz.
Hydrographic Buoy N-24 is transmitting methane tide telemetry,

17
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,080
[3,890 kHz CW telemetry & metallic buoy bell clank]

18
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:50,420
though migratory silt-striders rubbing against the guy-wires
just detuned the whip antenna by 18 Hertz. eQSL #0882 logged.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,080
Preset One—Callisto Dome Four, 11,410 kilohertz.
Unlicensed noodle-market broadcaster Radio Corrugated,

20
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:00,580
[11,410 kHz AM night-market lute & dipole blowtorch spike]

21
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:05,760
peaking at S9+10 right as their engineer hit the rooftop dipole with a blowtorch.

22
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:12,651
Preset Three—extragalactic, 1,420 MHz on the hydrogen line,
2.7 million light-years toward M-33.

23
00:02:12,691 --> 00:02:18,538
No video carrier on this band—just a relativistic Doppler Lissajous on the spectrum scan.

24
00:02:18,578 --> 00:02:30,380
Running Translation Algorithm 02 against the raw hex stream decodes Buoy M-33-771:
still issuing small-craft advisories for an ammonia sea that evaporated during the Ming Dynasty.

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,885
And on Preset Four, 6,925 kilohertz in the Jupiter Trojans:
an encrypted base-eight numbers station

26
00:02:36,925 --> 00:02:46,880
where Algorithm 03 just decoded six metric tons of pork-chive dumpling wrappers—
plus an octal shift key of 13 for those tracking the sector cipher in the station log.

27
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:56,779
Quick check on the Bogey-Nine Perimeter Trail-Cam,
which discriminates ballistic Oort rocks from non-Keplerian visitors right outside our cliff rim.

28
00:02:56,819 --> 00:03:06,334
At 03:41 Galactic, Trail-Cam One on the Acheron North Rim triggered an eight-frame burst
on a mirror-chrome cylinder drifting between two tumbling boulders at 14 m/s—

29
00:03:06,374 --> 00:03:16,580
before executing a 90-degree vertical snap-turn on Frame Five at 140g with zero thruster plume.
The Outer Belt Safety Board says it was a vented thermos flask from the Mess Hall.

30
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:27,272
Now to our centerpiece instrument: the Van Allen ED-9 Euclidean Detector—
searching for geometric intelligence across the universe.

31
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:36,711
Natural vacuum produces fractals and thermal static;
intelligence leaves straight lines, parallel chords, and constructive ratios.

32
00:03:36,751 --> 00:03:49,200
Tonight, our 12-tube Hough Transform correlator locked onto a single 99.998% synthetic signature
in Callisto-South Brine Evaporation Vat 19: the Unsuspecting Parallelogram.

33
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:59,665
Under inspection-beam sweep Frame Seven, four salt-crust ridges form parallelogram ABDC—
satisfying Euclid Book One, Proposition 34:

34
00:03:59,705 --> 00:04:11,150
opposite sides AB and CD, and AC and BD, hold parallel to 0.0002 arcseconds,
while diagonal diameter BC bisects the brine sludge into two congruent triangles.

35
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:21,543
Seven minutes after our Van Allen detector logged the Proposition 34 proof,
the Callisto Water Board scrubbed the archive and blamed a motorized mud-rake that lost a cotter pin.

36
00:04:21,583 --> 00:04:24,410
That is one remarkably well-educated mud-rake, folks.

37
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:34,251
On the next broadcast: an uninspected Dilithium barge rendezvous in the tail of Comet K-Four,
and a suspected rhombus aboard a bulk ice-hauler.

38
00:04:34,291 --> 00:04:41,809
This broadcast is underwritten by Van Allen and Sons Switchgear—
from radiation belts to reactor beds, if it arcs, we clamp it.

39
00:04:41,849 --> 00:04:47,820
From Asteroid 3-5-1 in Oort Cloud Sector 9, this is GOR-9—
your eye to the cosmos, ear to the vacuum.

40
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:48,910
[Harmonic crystal sign-off chime]

41
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:49,260
[Carrier transitions to O.R.S. 351 orbital downlink]

42
00:04:50,110 --> 00:04:56,431
Remember, a like indication on your listening apparatus
gives us three kilowatts of Dilithium reserve,

43
00:04:56,471 --> 00:05:01,420
and a subscription gets us one step closer
to shielding our marzelvane emitters.

44
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:08,760
[Soft Lydian harmonic chime & orbital carrier]
